  "material_learning": "Lagged high-VIX avoidance is a real historical risk-state effect but not a sufficiently stable risk-adjusted BTC strategy. The primary reduced Validation drawdown from 32.28416349 to 26.56660237 percent and still returned 324.58451899 percent after Normal costs, but passive BTC returned 464.75475156 percent. Its Validation Calmar was only 84.870642 percent of passive and annual Calmar was non-worse in only 2020 and 2022. The stricter 0.7 neighbor captured only 53.134246 percent of Validation upside and reached only 57.122616 percent of passive Calmar. Thus drawdown reduction was purchased with too much missed upside, while neighbor stability failed.",
